{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/960420-the-vigil-behind-mass-media","id":960420,"title":"The Vigil behind Mass Media","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-30T07:20:20-07:00","id":960420,"title":"The Vigil behind Mass Media","content":"Considering how much strangeness can be found in the Chronicles of Darkness, proof of the supernatural should have reached the public a long time ago. Especially now, in the age of mass media, a team of resourceful hunters will occasionally try to blow everything wide open. Why didn't they succeed, then? The many conspiracies make sure troublesome voices are either silenced or drowned in a sea of irrelevance. As you go higher, you get more factions using media for their own purposes, more champions for a cause, more crusaders for the bottom line. Then, there's the supernatural. In the Chronicles of Darkness, media can't be sanitized - they should be a pressure cooker.<br /> <br /> Please, share your thoughts, plot hooks and factions.<br /> <br /> Here comes Bobby<br /> <br /> It's 28th of February, 1983. The scheduled programming is interrupted by a transmission from the studio. A blank-eyed young man is seen arguing with the staff, later to turn to the audience and announce &quot;Here comes Bobby&quot;. A moment afterwards, around the country, everyone in front of their TV set suffers a massive seizure. The following days are hectic. With millions of dead or unresponsive, the government goes on high alert. The Soviet Union is quick to deny involvement, but skyrocketing paranoia makes a hot war a real possibility. The authorities apprehend the intruder. They uncover a history of abuse and mental illness but fail to gain any coherent information. The next day none of that ever happened. The show went as planned. There was no intruder, not to mention a national catastrophe. However, about a dozen of studio employees wake with clear memories of the days that weren't and confused, fearful memories of the <i>other</i> interloper. One of the workers manages to track the boy's house, but after finding flashing lights of police cars on the scene, doesn't have the nerve to follow through. The unlucky few try to resume their lives. They mostly succeed, but they don't forget.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T10:35:05-07:00","id":960533,"title":"","content":"Are you asking for revelation hooks or cover-up hooks? I can't tell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12243-dreaming-cat","name":"Dreaming Cat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T11:05:46-07:00","id":960552,"title":"","content":"A basic assumption of the setting is that a revelation is unlikely to succeed. At least not globally and not in the long term. It still leaves room for partial success. Seeing how it fails is also an interesting journey. That doesn't matter, though. If you have something - share it!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T17:55:34-07:00","id":960768,"title":"","content":"Each major cable news network has at least one cell on the inside, most actually don't link up with compacts, believing these groups don't understand the damage mass revelation could do. Others are quickly subverted by massive compacts, becoming the censors of the paranormal and conspiratorial within these companies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T22:59:40-07:00","id":960900,"title":"","content":"You're thinking in 1E. In 2E terms there's no conspiracy keeping monsters of the mass media but<br /> <br /> 1) if you put them there most mortals will change the channel<br /> 2) If you're talking about a specific monster they might &quot;object&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T08:55:36-07:00","id":961075,"title":"","content":"It's true that I didn't account for Mortal mentality, but by dismissing this idea out of hand you're missing out on many plot hooks. If someone regenerates, let's say, Rick Allen's arm on live TV it's bound to have some impact, even if just among rock music aficionados. It's the fraction of Mortals who do not ignore the event that is relevant for the story. I wasn't implying there is a single conspiracy, either. Guardians of the Veil will make damn sure that the rare Supernal Verge doesn't become a tourist attraction, even if nobody claims it's truly supernatural. Invictus will be in an uproar if one of their puppets becomes an object of a smear campaign, even if they're a normal human. It's exactly because some monster might object, why media must be brimming with multiple supernatural interests. Objections will do them no good after their home address is revealed. Also, let's say, Mouth of the Depths won't drag itself miles away from the ocean to enact its revenge. If media people know better that to share such information, it's fun to know how they learned that and what else is going on.<br /> <br /> Some might consider this secrecy an unrealistic idea, but accept it as a necessary premise of the game. That involves ignoring all the stress lines. I think it would be much more fun to explore this area. It will even strengthen the premise of the game by showing how secrecy reinforces itself. I am certain there should be supernatural interests all around the media, as much as I am certain wizards screen the National Lottery winners for magical talent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":7593,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","user":"Teatime","date":". 08-31-2016, 12:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}